<body>
    <h1>Final Exam Announcement</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"toc-macro">
<a href=3D"#FinalExamAnnouncement-ExamStructure">Exam Structure</a> | <a hr=
ef=3D"#FinalExamAnnouncement-Submission">Submission</a> | <a href=3D"#Final=
ExamAnnouncement-Timeline">Timeline</a>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"FinalExamAnnouncement-ExamStructure">Exam Structure</h1>
<p>We have already prepared the container image for the web application. Th=
e images and their environment variables are: (Repo link: <a class=3D"exter=
nal-link" href=3D"https://hub.docker.com/u/cuongopswat" rel=3D"nofollow">ht=
tps://hub.docker.com/u/cuongopswat</a>)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>cuongopswat/go-coffeeshop-web</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>REVERSE_PROXY_URL: &lt;proxy_service:port&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>WEB_PORT: 8888</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>cuongopswat/go-coffeeshop-proxy</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>APP_NAME: &lt;Any Name&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>GRPC_PRODUCT_HOST: &lt;product service&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>GRPC_PRODUCT_PORT: 5001</p></li>
<li>
<p>GRPC_COUNTER_HOST: &lt;counter service&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>GRPC_COUNTER_PORT: 5002</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>cuongopswat/go-coffeeshop-barista</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>APP_NAME: &lt;Any Name&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>IN_DOCKER: "true"</p></li>
<li>
<p>PG_URL: &lt;Postgresql connection string&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>PG_DSN_URL: &lt;host=3D=E2=80=A6 user=3D=E2=80=A6 password=3D=E2=80=A6 d=
bname=3D=E2=80=A6 sslmode=3Ddisable&gt; sslmode=3Ddisable</p></li>
<li>
<p>RABBITMQ_URL: &lt;RabbitMQ connection string&gt;</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>cuongopswat/go-coffeeshop-kitchen</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>APP_NAME: &lt;Any Name&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>IN_DOCKER: "true"</p></li>
<li>
<p>PG_URL: &lt;Postgresql connection string&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>PG_DSN_URL: &lt;host=3D=E2=80=A6 user=3D=E2=80=A6 password=3D=E2=80=A6 d=
bname=3D=E2=80=A6 sslmode=3Ddisable&gt; sslmode=3Ddisable</p></li>
<li>
<p>RABBITMQ_URL: &lt;RabbitMQ connection string&gt;</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>cuongopswat/go-coffeeshop-counter</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>APP_NAME:&lt;Any Name&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>IN_DOCKER: "true"</p></li>
<li>
<p>PG_URL: &lt;Postgresql connection string&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>PG_DSN_URL: &lt;host=3D=E2=80=A6 user=3D=E2=80=A6 password=3D=E2=80=A6 d=
bname=3D=E2=80=A6 sslmode=3Ddisable&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>RABBITMQ_URL: &lt;RabbitMQ connection string&gt;</p></li>
<li>
<p>PRODUCT_CLIENT_URL: &lt;product-service:port&gt;</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>cuongopswat/go-coffeeshop-product</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>APP_NAME: &lt;Any Name&gt;</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>postgres:14-alpine</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>POSTGRES_DB</p></li>
<li>
<p>POSTGRES_USER</p></li>
<li>
<p>POSTGRES_PASSWORD</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>rabbitmq:3.11-management-alpine</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER</p></li>
<li>
<p>RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Start order:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>PostgreSQL:</p></li>
<li>
<p>RabbitMQ:</p></li>
<li>
<p>Product</p></li>
<li>
<p>Counter</p></li>
<li>
<p>The remaining services</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Port expose:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Postgresql: 5432</p></li>
<li>
<p>RabbiMQ: 5672 and 15672</p></li>
<li>
<p>proxy: 5000</p></li>
<li>
<p>product: 5001</p></li>
<li>
<p>counter: 5002</p></li>
<li>
<p>web: 8888</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Here is your exam:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"960" data-layout=3D"wide" data-local-id=3D"cc05c=
a97-1b0e-4d0e-a580-0a39b10acf1a" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col>
<col style=3D"width: 216.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 130.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 103.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 469.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTh"></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Section</strong></p>
<p></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Subsection</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Weight</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Requirement</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">1</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Preparation</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>&nbsp;</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The infrastructure is hosted on AWS which can be used with a personal or=
 the OPSWAT Devops training account.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Your code should be stored on any VCS such as GitHub, Gitlab=E2=80=A6 It=
=E2=80=99s supposed to share your code with the examiner</p></li>
</ol></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">2</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Infrastructure as code</p>
<p>(Terraform and awscli)</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>&nbsp;</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>20%</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Resources: (You should read the full exam to clarify all the requirement=
s for each resource)</p></li>
<li>
<p>All resources are created by Terraform or AWS CLI.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Public modules are allowed, but not with basic infrastructure (VPC, Subn=
et, SG)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use a different workspace for each environment.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Using remote S3 backend.</p></li>
</ol></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">3</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" rowspan=3D"4" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Application deployment</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Prepare</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Pull the above images and push to your Docker private registry</p>
<p>(You can change the image name if you want)</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">4</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Dev environment</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>10%</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Create the EC2 and install Docker</p></li>
<li>
<p>Prepare Docker-Compose to deploy the dev environment</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure healthcheck settings</p></li>
</ol></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">5</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Prod environment</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>20%</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Create the EKS cluster with minimal resource capacity</p></li>
<li>
<p>Create in-cluster resources by the Declarative method.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Create YAML files for all resources</p></li>
<li>
<p>Create a Horizontal Pod Autoscaling to apply scale</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensuring security both at rest and in transit.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure healthcheck settings</p></li>
</ol></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">6</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Database</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>10%</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Using Postgresql by using RDS (use Free-tier option, t3.micro, no HA, no=
 read-replica setup), ensure using Secret Manager to store sensitive data</=
p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">7</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>CI/CD</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>&nbsp;</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>20%</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>CI/CD pipeline (can choose AWS CodePipeline or TeamCity, or Github Actio=
ns) to support application integration and delivery. The pipeline should be=
:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Scan the image with the Trivy software</p></li>
<li>
<p>Push the image to the Docker private registry</p></li>
<li>
<p>Deploy the application with the latest image, can choose one of the 2 me=
chanisms below:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>(Optional) Using Argocd to apply the GitOps pull mechanism.</p></li>
<li>
<p>(Optional) Using Helm/Kubeclt to apply the GitOps push mechanism.</p></l=
i>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>(You can spin up a new EC2 to deploy TeamCity and Argocd for your own)</=
p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd">8</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Monitoring System</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>&nbsp;</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>20%</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Monitoring system (can choose to use Amazon CloudWatch/Grafana) to monit=
or the system.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A dashboard to monitor: Nodes CPU and Memory, Pods CPU and Memory, API r=
equests, 4xx, 5xx http requests.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Alert if:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The autoscaling scales to the maximum number.</p></li>
<li>
<p>There=E2=80=99s an anomaly change in the ELB=E2=80=99s RequestCount.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>High memory or CPU usage in any component of application</p></li>
<li>
<p>5xx errors</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"FinalExamAnnouncement-Submission">Submission</h1>
<p>There are 2 parts:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Provide your repository with a friendly format README to describ=
e the solution for the exam requirement, including sections</strong>:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Summary: Describe the summary of the solution.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Architecture: The architecture of the solution.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Component description: The Description of each component in the architec=
ture.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The homepage of the application</p></li>
<li>
<p>User guideline: The guideline on how to use the source code to provision=
/deploy components in the architecture.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Demonstration</strong>:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>DevOps Intern Learners</strong>: offline demonstration with 30-4=
5 minutes per person.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Regular Learners (not DevOps Intern)</strong>: a short video to =
demonstrate your deployment. You can cut the deployment progress because it=
 takes a long time to complete.</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p>Once done, you can <strong>send your submission to</strong> <a class=3D"=
external-link" href=3D"mailto:cuong.tran@opswat.com" rel=3D"nofollow">cuong=
.tran@opswat.com</a>.</p>
<h1 id=3D"FinalExamAnnouncement-Timeline">Timeline</h1>
<ul>
<li>
<p>For Regular Learners, submission deadline: <time datetime=3D"2025-05-20"=
 class=3D"date-past">20 May 2025</time></p></li>
<li>
<p>For DevOps Intern Learners, demonstration date: <time datetime=3D"2025-0=
5-20" class=3D"date-past">20 May 2025</time></p></li>
<li>
<p>Trainer team=E2=80=99s evaluation: from <time datetime=3D"2025-05-21" cl=
ass=3D"date-past">21 May 2025</time> to <time datetime=3D"2025-05-28" class=
=3D"date-past">28 May 2025</time></p></li>
<li>
<p>Result announcement: <time datetime=3D"2025-05-29" class=3D"date-past">2=
9 May 2025</time></p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
